    /// <c>Wblock</c>): closed multilines (the square of 100, a triangle, a six-sided staircase) of STANDARD at scale 20
    /// justified at the top. Each row is the points of the multiline, the MLEDIT cut (CA cuts all elements, CS one) with its
    /// two picks, the vertex and where it goes, then the multiline before and after as its flags and its vertices with the
    /// stretches of each element after the offset in braces: <c>(0,0){0,30,60}{0}</c> is the vertex (0, 0) whose first element
